Hi everybody.

4
00:00:06.565 --> 00:00:07.527
Hi.

5
00:00:07.527 --> 00:00:09.087
Oh, your hair is so long!

6
00:00:09.087 --> 00:00:12.703
I know, my hair is ridiculously long.

7
00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:13.536
Hi friend.

8
00:00:13.536 --> 00:00:14.495
Ooh, you worked out.

9
00:00:14.495 --> 00:00:15.500
Oh gosh.

10
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.410
My children are large, Drew.

11
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.620
And you have two boys.

12
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.453
I do.

13
00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:22.280
And my two and a half year old's a giant.

14
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.113
Okay.

15
00:00:23.113 --> 00:00:25.620
So the last time you came here was like,

16
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.960
the morning after the insurrection.

17
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.830
It was the morning after the insurrection.

18
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.830
And here we are, in the middle of a new war.

19
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.810
And how do we persevere?

20
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.040
How do we go about are days

21
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.819
when such difficult things are happening?

22
00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:45.850
Oh gosh, Drew.

23
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.030
Well, there is a lot happening.

24
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.740
I mean, here in our city of New York,

25
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.808
across our country and certainly around the world.

26
00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:59.040 line:15%
We see the ongoing humanitarian crisis in Ukraine.

27
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.300 line:15%
Although we know that Ukraine isn't

28
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.691 line:15%
the only country in the world that is under

29
00:01:03.691 --> 00:01:07.401 line:15%
kind of war and violence and kind of threat

30
00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:10.948
from outside or inside.

31
00:01:10.948 --> 00:01:15.948
And I think either we can drown in the despair

32
00:01:16.013 --> 00:01:20.067
or we can decide to try to do something about it.

33
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.440
And I think there is a lot that we can do.

34
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.110
I mean, for those of us, with resources,

35
00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.660
we can donate to the international rescue committee,

36
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.110
and so many of the amazing organizations

37
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.280
who are on the front lines trying to give people food

38
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.630
and medical support and hope.

39
00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.788
We can put continued pressure,

40
00:01:37.788 --> 00:01:41.660
kind of especially for those of us who live in democracies,

41
00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.594
to have a unified effort to stand up to Putin

42
00:01:45.594 --> 00:01:48.462
and all of his brutality,

43
00:01:48.462 --> 00:01:52.768
because I think ultimately, Drew, optimism is a moral choice

44
00:01:52.768 --> 00:01:55.930
and I think it is the more moral choice

45
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.810
to choose to be optimistic, to choose to believe

46
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.453
that our efforts and our energies can make a difference,

47
00:02:02.453 --> 00:02:05.100
because otherwise we just all like put our covers

48
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.180
over our heads and I don't think that's gonna

49
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.780
make us feel very good.

50
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.740
Right, I think that's then just seeding to hopelessness.

51
00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.460
I would much rather try to act hopeful

52
00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.270
and try to create more hope in the world.

53
00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.850
So, that happiness you talk about is hard,

54
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.500
one, because we know we have all tried to do our part.

55
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.880
And you just did it.

56
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.139
You just did it.

57
00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:28.139
(audience applause)

58
00:02:31.357 --> 00:02:34.175
I always love that you and I also,

59
00:02:34.175 --> 00:02:37.610
and I cannot hold a candle to your experience

60
00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.540
growing up in front of everybody.

61
00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.780
I just, I love asking you life advice

62
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.762
because as you are very full of grace

63
00:02:46.762 --> 00:02:49.342
and I don't know, how do you do it?

64
00:02:49.342 --> 00:02:52.040
How do you remain this full of grace

65
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.120
while the world is difficult,

66
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.290
while people are divided or different?

67
00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.510
What's your one foot in front of the other?

68
00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.180
Well, I think being myself, somewhat stubbornly.

69
00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.000
I'm terrible at being other people.

70
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.200
But I just am not an actress.

71
00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.050
I don't have those jeans like you do.

72
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.240
And I can't do it in real life.

73
00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.270
I can't fake anything.

74
00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.573
I can't fake anything.

75
00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:19.090
And yet then I do know I have to take care of myself

76
00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:22.260
so that I can hopefully take care of others,

77
00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.590
the others in kind of the smaller world of my family

78
00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.940
and the others in the bigger sense of the work

79
00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.030
that I feel called to do,

80
00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.210
whether as a as an author or an advocate.

81
00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.840
So I spend a lot of time with my kids

82
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.100
because they just bring me so much joy.

83
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.160
And I spend a lot of time running

84
00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.130
because I find running is like my meditative space.

85
00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.530
And I'm also, I'm quite religious.

86
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.480
And I was able to finally go back in person to church

87
00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.010
a few weeks ago, which meant a huge amount to me

88
00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.900
to be able to be kind of in the sanctuary,

89
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.230
was a very different experience than livestream.

90
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.800
Although like God bless my minister

91
00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.230
for just never giving up on those of us

92
00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.450
on the other side of the screen,

93
00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.700
who she couldn't see or kind of be with

94
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.910
in kind of physical community.

95
00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.308
And so all of that really matters to me

96
00:04:10.308 --> 00:04:13.100
and is then how I try to help remind myself

97
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.300
that I do matter.

98
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.350
So then I can try to do more work that I hope

99
00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:20.690
creates more more possibility for more people

100
00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.820
and more places.

101
00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.065
And you do.

102
00:04:23.065 --> 00:04:25.290
(audience applause)

103
00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.650
Church, running, stubbornly being yourself.

104
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:32.930
All three of those things seem doable,

105
00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.460
attainable, admirable.

106
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.620
When you move your body, you do shift your chemistry.

107
00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.287 line:15%
